-- where_variable_unbound (§10.6 trigger (b), 8:24 and 8:27): the closure
-- rule of §2.4 — `x` and `s` occur only inside the constraint's type, so
-- they are not quantified by the annotation, have no place in the
-- canonical evidence order (§7.2) and are refused here rather than
-- silently disagreed about at the first call. One message per offending
-- variable, at its first occurrence.
pub total : List a → a
    where a.fold : a, (x, s → s), s → s
total xs = xs
